WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:01.009
- What's up, y'all?

00:00:01.009 --> 00:00:03.211
I'm back with Nico Santos, give it up!

00:00:03.211 --> 00:00:05.155
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:00:05.155 --> 00:00:06.709
So from time to time, it's really nice

00:00:06.709 --> 00:00:09.465
to get out of the studio
and see people face to face

00:00:09.465 --> 00:00:11.619
even if it's from a safe social distance.

00:00:11.619 --> 00:00:13.120
So I've been hitting the road

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.557
to get to the outdoor theater

00:00:14.557 --> 00:00:18.140
for what we call a
drive-interview. Get it?

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:22.534
♪ Drive interview ♪

00:00:23.581 --> 00:00:26.581
Did you hear Jesse? Jesse with
the view, he was impressed.

00:00:26.581 --> 00:00:27.414
(laughing)

00:00:27.414 --> 00:00:28.936
The other day, I was hanging out

00:00:28.936 --> 00:00:32.227
when the very funny Jesse
Tyler Ferguson pulled in.

00:00:32.227 --> 00:00:34.824
I love that I'm just hanging
out randomly by myself

00:00:34.824 --> 00:00:36.325
(chuckles)

00:00:36.325 --> 00:00:38.245
and Jesse Tyler just happened to pull in.

00:00:38.245 --> 00:00:40.667
It was so random, take a look.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:43.250
(upbeat music)

00:00:51.525 --> 00:00:52.853
- [Jesse] Come on, grandma.

00:00:52.853 --> 00:00:56.235
- What's up. What's up?
How you doing, Jesse?

00:00:56.235 --> 00:00:57.653
- I love it, I love the car.

00:00:57.653 --> 00:00:58.933
- Um, I like your car.

00:00:58.933 --> 00:01:00.823
- It's a, it's a model red.

00:01:00.823 --> 00:01:02.147
- It's a model red?

00:01:02.147 --> 00:01:03.225
- I don't know anything about cars.

00:01:03.225 --> 00:01:04.240
(chuckling)

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.821
- You know, you don't like
classic cars or anything?

00:01:05.821 --> 00:01:07.805
- I don't. And actually,
the closest I have

00:01:07.805 --> 00:01:11.809
to any sort of like classic car
thing anywhere near my house

00:01:11.809 --> 00:01:15.869
is this horse sculpture
that Justin and I bought

00:01:15.869 --> 00:01:18.410
that's entirely made of
car parts and bike parts.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:19.243
- Oh.

00:01:19.243 --> 00:01:21.000
- That's the only thing that I have

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.160
in the classic car category in my house.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.360
- (chuckles) That's funny.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.799
Wait, speaking of houses,
you're in Gwyn's house.

00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:27.632
- I am, yes.

00:01:27.632 --> 00:01:30.026
- Yeah, you got Gwen Stefani's house.

00:01:30.026 --> 00:01:31.146
- Yes. She lived there for,

00:01:31.146 --> 00:01:32.765
I don't know like seven or eight years,

00:01:32.765 --> 00:01:35.277
but yeah. It's got good
energy because of her.

00:01:35.277 --> 00:01:37.365
- Oh, wow. Right on, right on.

00:01:37.365 --> 00:01:40.426
Um, how is your little one?

00:01:40.426 --> 00:01:42.013
Because, how old, how old now?

00:01:42.013 --> 00:01:43.397
- [Jesse] He's seven months now.

00:01:43.397 --> 00:01:44.956
- I was gonna say he
hasn't had a first birthday

00:01:44.956 --> 00:01:46.182
because I did see the shower.

00:01:46.182 --> 00:01:47.842
- [Jesse] Yes.
- The shower was incredible.

00:01:47.842 --> 00:01:49.432
- In February, it was the last party

00:01:49.432 --> 00:01:51.992
that anyone went to in the
world. It was our baby shower.

00:01:51.992 --> 00:01:54.430
- That's kind of a cool one to go out on.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:57.158
It was quite a blow out and
we didn't plan it ourselves.

00:01:57.158 --> 00:01:58.180
We had a friend of ours plan it,

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.721
and the venue that they
rented had a swimming pool.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:04.660
So we hired this group of
male synchronized swimmers

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:06.910
called um, the Aquawillies.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:10.018
- W-w-w-what?

00:02:10.018 --> 00:02:12.809
- Aquawillies, and they were amazing.

00:02:12.809 --> 00:02:14.830
And they were, they were a
complete surprise to us, but...

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.247
- That's amazing.

00:02:18.142 --> 00:02:19.702
How's it been, being a dad?

00:02:19.702 --> 00:02:22.241
- It's been, it's been great. I love it.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.201
- It's exhausting.

00:02:23.201 --> 00:02:24.921
- It is so exhausting and the thing is

00:02:24.921 --> 00:02:26.279
Beckett was born in July

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.720
and for like the first
three months, I was like

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.209
I'm so grateful to have this,

00:02:29.209 --> 00:02:30.793
this time when I'm not working to just,

00:02:30.793 --> 00:02:32.442
you know, spend time with him.
- Yeah.

00:02:32.442 --> 00:02:34.452
And now I really, really, really wish

00:02:34.452 --> 00:02:37.492
I could just like slip away
and go to work for the day.

00:02:37.492 --> 00:02:38.325
- Yeah.

00:02:38.325 --> 00:02:40.446
- Julie, Julie Bowen and Ty
Burrell would always like,

00:02:40.446 --> 00:02:42.745
stay in their trailer
a little while longer

00:02:42.745 --> 00:02:45.227
after they were done shooting
and just like get naps in.

00:02:45.227 --> 00:02:46.686
And I have no, I can't do that.

00:02:46.686 --> 00:02:49.046
I can't just disappear
and take a nap somewhere.

00:02:49.046 --> 00:02:51.438
- You will, you will get there.

00:02:51.438 --> 00:02:53.197
(laughing)

00:02:53.197 --> 00:02:54.030
- I'm just gonna lie down.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.107
- You will totally get there and be like,

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:56.137
man it was so weird,

00:02:56.137 --> 00:02:58.426
work went a little longer than suspected.

00:02:58.426 --> 00:02:59.259
- [Jesse] Yeah, yeah.

00:02:59.259 --> 00:03:01.080
Meanwhile, you're just
sitting in your car.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.773
- They're like, how was the
chat with Kelly Clarkson,

00:03:02.773 --> 00:03:04.282
you were, you were there a long time.

00:03:04.282 --> 00:03:05.581
I'm like sleeping in
the back of this thing.

00:03:05.581 --> 00:03:07.962
- Well, I'm chatty. You can
blame it on that. I talk a lot.

00:03:07.962 --> 00:03:09.159
(chuckles)

00:03:09.159 --> 00:03:10.522
I found this amazing.

00:03:10.522 --> 00:03:12.141
So, you came out with a cookbook, right?

00:03:12.141 --> 00:03:13.794
- Yeah. I have a cooking partner.

00:03:13.794 --> 00:03:15.311
Her name is Julie Tanous.

00:03:15.311 --> 00:03:18.309
She and I met at a dinner
party like six years ago.

00:03:18.309 --> 00:03:20.831
She has taught me how to
do so much in the kitchen.

00:03:20.831 --> 00:03:23.300
And so, we, we wrote a cookbook together

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.082
and it's um, we've been working
on it for like two years.

00:03:26.082 --> 00:03:27.382
It's called Food Between Friends.

00:03:27.382 --> 00:03:28.560
- What a great title.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.490
- Yeah. It's been really fun. Yeah.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.231
- So, you love food. You're a foodie.

00:03:32.231 --> 00:03:35.469
So, how is your little one, Beckett?

00:03:35.469 --> 00:03:37.019
How is he with food?

00:03:37.019 --> 00:03:40.069
- [Jesse] He's, he's
actually a little picky, um,

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:41.360
which is concerning to me.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.251
- Welcome to having a boy.
- [Jesse] Yeah. (chuckles)

00:03:42.251 --> 00:03:44.571
- Because my girl will eat anything,

00:03:44.571 --> 00:03:45.893
I could bribe her to eat anything.

00:03:45.893 --> 00:03:48.963
And, my boy eats anything beige.

00:03:48.963 --> 00:03:50.581
- Ours is a, if it's a tiniest little,

00:03:50.581 --> 00:03:52.912
if it has the tiniest little
bit of flavor, he's like, no.

00:03:52.912 --> 00:03:54.203
- Yeah, and he freaks out.

00:03:54.203 --> 00:03:55.122
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:55.122 --> 00:03:56.773
- [Kelly] Have you ever
gone too spicy with food?

00:03:56.773 --> 00:03:58.213
Have you ever been making
something and you...

00:03:58.213 --> 00:04:00.691
- I mean, I, I love Mexican food and I,

00:04:00.691 --> 00:04:03.212
I have gone too spicy with that actually.

00:04:03.212 --> 00:04:05.312
And it, it happened with my older age.

00:04:05.312 --> 00:04:07.200
I'm 45 now, and like five years ago,

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.861
I remember lying in bed like,

00:04:08.861 --> 00:04:10.320
Oh my God, I think I'm
having a heart attack.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.853
And I actually went to the hospital

00:04:11.853 --> 00:04:13.883
and it was just acid reflux.

00:04:13.883 --> 00:04:16.021
I'm like, oh, that's
something I have to deal with.

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:17.371
(audience laughing)

00:04:17.371 --> 00:04:18.504
- Did you feel like such a tool?

00:04:18.504 --> 00:04:19.672
- I felt like such an idiot.

00:04:19.672 --> 00:04:21.042
They're like, you're just a little gassy.

00:04:21.042 --> 00:04:21.931
- They're like, so you have heartburn.

00:04:21.931 --> 00:04:22.792
- [Jesse] Yeah.

00:04:22.792 --> 00:04:24.144
(laughs) So embarrassing.

00:04:24.144 --> 00:04:25.523
They like prescribed me Tums.

00:04:25.523 --> 00:04:26.356
- It's life threatening, help me.

00:04:26.356 --> 00:04:27.624
(laughs)

00:04:27.624 --> 00:04:28.544
That was amazing.

00:04:28.544 --> 00:04:30.184
Well, I love seeing you.

00:04:30.184 --> 00:04:31.091
- [Jesse] It's so good to see you.

00:04:31.091 --> 00:04:32.052
- And I loved hanging out with you.

00:04:32.052 --> 00:04:34.703
- Before, I leave though, you um,

00:04:34.703 --> 00:04:36.001
I know you work with Blake.

00:04:36.001 --> 00:04:39.000
I do actually have some
of Gwen's, um, mail.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.895
I'm still getting at the
house, catalogs and stuff.

00:04:40.895 --> 00:04:41.728
- Oh, yeah.

00:04:41.728 --> 00:04:42.700
- So, I don't know if like,

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.388
- Oh, that's a box, it's a box.

00:04:44.388 --> 00:04:45.221
Yeah.

00:04:45.221 --> 00:04:46.054
Yeah.

00:04:46.054 --> 00:04:46.887
Oh.

00:04:46.887 --> 00:04:47.837
- [Jesse] Bring that over to her.

00:04:47.837 --> 00:04:48.752
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:48.752 --> 00:04:50.740
That's a box of stuff. Okay.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:51.573
- So good to see you.

00:04:51.573 --> 00:04:53.083
- It's nice to see you.

00:04:53.083 --> 00:04:55.643
I will get that to them.

00:04:55.643 --> 00:04:57.584
(car honks)

00:04:57.584 --> 00:05:00.167
(upbeat music)

00:05:02.555 --> 00:05:03.722
- [Jesse] Bye.

00:05:04.563 --> 00:05:05.773
(audience cheers and claps)

00:05:05.773 --> 00:05:08.312
- Aren't, wait, what about you?
Do you like cooking at home?

00:05:08.312 --> 00:05:11.285
- Uh, yeah, I've done nothing
but cook during quarantine

00:05:11.285 --> 00:05:14.093
which is why I've gained like, 700 pounds.

00:05:14.093 --> 00:05:14.926
(laughs)

00:05:14.926 --> 00:05:17.142
- Honestly, I gained
because I didn't cook.

00:05:17.142 --> 00:05:18.792
I Postmated a lot. (chuckles)

00:05:18.792 --> 00:05:20.743
- Well, that too. We would
cook and then Postmates

00:05:20.743 --> 00:05:21.681
and the cycle continues.

00:05:21.681 --> 00:05:22.514
- Do you like cooking?

00:05:22.514 --> 00:05:23.347
- I love cooking.

00:05:23.347 --> 00:05:25.544
I, my boyfriend is the savory
cook and I'm more of a baker.

00:05:25.544 --> 00:05:26.565
- [Kelly] Oh, what a team.

00:05:26.565 --> 00:05:28.712
- I know, it's great. It's great. (laughs)

00:05:28.712 --> 00:05:31.470
- I'm just alone. Just
cooking for me, so. (laughs)

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:32.475
Just kidding, no,

00:05:32.475 --> 00:05:34.643
I, it doesn't matter if
people are there or not.

00:05:34.643 --> 00:05:35.522
I can't cook.

00:05:35.522 --> 00:05:38.005
Um, don't forget to
pick up Jesse's new book

00:05:38.005 --> 00:05:39.033
Food Between Friends.

